* Pigeonhole principle: 3 pigeons, 2 holes
* Each pigeon must be in at least one hole
* Each hole can have at most one pigeon
* UNSAT
* #variable= 6 #constraint= 5
* Variables: p_i_j means pigeon i is in hole j
* p11=x1, p12=x2, p21=x3, p22=x4, p31=x5, p32=x6
* Pigeon 1 in some hole: x1 + x2 >= 1
+1 x1 +1 x2 >= 1 ;
* Pigeon 2 in some hole: x3 + x4 >= 1
+1 x3 +1 x4 >= 1 ;
* Pigeon 3 in some hole: x5 + x6 >= 1
+1 x5 +1 x6 >= 1 ;
* Hole 1 has at most 1 pigeon: ~x1 + ~x3 + ~x5 >= 2
+1 ~x1 +1 ~x3 +1 ~x5 >= 2 ;
* Hole 2 has at most 1 pigeon: ~x2 + ~x4 + ~x6 >= 2
+1 ~x2 +1 ~x4 +1 ~x6 >= 2 ;
